skill: "ffmpeg-video-editor"
sections[18]:
  - "\n"
  - "# FFmpeg Video Editor\n\nProgrammatic video assembly, EDL rendering, and audio post-production engine for local shell workflows. Replaces manual graphical timeline tasks with deterministic, reproducible FFmpeg commands.\n\n"
  - "## Production-Correctness Hard Rules\n\n1. **Subtitles LAST**: Always burn subtitles after all overlays and B-roll so graphics never cover captions.\n2. **Per-Segment Extract -> Lossless Concat**: Extract and grade each EDL segment individually, then `-c copy` concat instead of double-encoding.\n3. **30ms Boundary Audio Fades**: Apply `afade=t=in:st=0:d=0.03,afade=t=out:st={dur-0.03}:d=0.03` on every cut segment to prevent audible clicks.\n4. **PTS-Shifted Overlays**: Apply `setpts=PTS-STARTPTS+T/TB` on overlay clips so frame 0 aligns with the overlay window start.\n5. **Output-Timeline SRT Remapping**: Remap word timestamps via `bin/agyos video edl-remap-srt` (`output_time = word.start - seg_start + seg_offset`).\n6. **Post-Render Self-Eval**: Verify duration, `ebur128` loudness, and `blackdetect` via `bin/agyos video self-eval`.\n\n"
  - "## AGYOS EDL & Timeline Commands\n\n```bash\n# Pack word-level transcript into compact phrase markdown\nbin/agyos video pack-transcript transcript.json --out takes_packed.md\n\n# Validate EDL and remap captions onto output timeline\nbin/agyos video edl-validate edl.json --check-files --json\nbin/agyos video edl-remap-srt edl.json transcript.json --out master.srt\n\n# Render EDL (dry-run plan, fast 720p preview, or full master)\nbin/agyos video edl-render edl.json -o preview.mp4 --preview\nbin/agyos video edl-render edl.json -o final.mp4\n\n# Inspect cut boundary filmstrip + waveform and run self-eval\nbin/agyos video timeline-view final.mp4 4.5 7.5 -o cut_check.png\nbin/agyos video self-eval final.mp4 --edl edl.json --json\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Audio Engineering for YouTube\n\nYouTube normalizes all video audio to **-14 LUFS integrated loudness** with a **-1.0 dB True Peak ceiling**. Audio mastered outside this target gets dynamically lowered by the platform.\n\n"
  - "### Two-Pass Loudness Normalization (-14 LUFS) & Measurement\n\nPass 1: Measure current audio profile\n```bash\nffmpeg -i input.mp4 -af loudnorm=I=-14:TP=-1.0:LRA=11:print_format=json -f null -\n```\n\nPass 2: Apply linear normalization with measured parameters (or run `uv run scripts/repair_ai_video.py audio input.mp4 -o output_normalized.mp4`)\n```bash\nffmpeg -i input.mp4 -af loudnorm=I=-14:TP=-1.0:LRA=11:\\\nmeasured_I=-21.4:\\\nmeasured_TP=-3.2:\\\nmeasured_LRA=9.1:\\\nmeasured_thresh=-32.0:\\\noffset=0.2:linear=true \\\n-c:v copy -c:a aac -b:a 192k output_normalized.mp4\n```\n\nVerify integrated loudness and true peak:\n```bash\nffmpeg -i output_normalized.mp4 -af ebur128=peak=true -f null -\n```\n\n"
  - "### Dynamic Background Music Ducking\n\nAutomatically attenuates background music by 18dB whenever narration is active using sidechain compression:\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -i voiceover.wav -i background_music.mp3 -filter_complex \\\n\"[1:a]volume=0.35[music_base]; \\\n [music_base][0:a]sidechaincompress=threshold=0.08:ratio=6:attack=20:release=300[ducked_music]; \\\n [0:a][ducked_music]amix=inputs=2:duration=first:dropout_transition=2[aout]\" \\\n-map \"[aout]\" -c:a aac -b:a 192k mixed_audio.mp4\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Footage Assembly & Timing Automation\n\n"
  - "### Automated Silence Removal\n\nDetects and strips dead air pauses longer than 400 milliseconds from talking head or screen recordings:\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -i raw_take.mp4 -af \"silencedetect=noise=-30dB:d=0.4\" -f null - 2> silence.log\n```\n\nRemove silence intervals using the `silenceremove` filter:\n```bash\nffmpeg -i raw_take.mp4 -af \"silenceremove=start_periods=1:start_duration=0.1:start_threshold=-30dB:stop_periods=-1:stop_duration=0.4:stop_threshold=-30dB\" -c:v copy tight_take.mp4\n```\n\n"
  - "### Dynamic 1.15x Zoom Punch-in\n\nCreates visual rhythm during single-camera talking head segments to emphasize key arguments without jump cuts:\n\n```bash\n# Smooth punch-in between second 5 and second 10\nffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf \\\n\"zoompan=z='if(between(it,5,10),1.15,1.0)':x='iw/2-(iw/zoom/2)':y='ih/2-(ih/zoom/2)':d=1:s=1920x1080:fps=30\" \\\n-c:a copy punch_in.mp4\n```\n\n"
  - "### Video Watermark Removal & Delogo Inpainting\n\nRemoves localized corner logos or watermarks using bilateral pixel interpolation:\n\n```bash\n# General syntax: delogo=x=<left>:y=<top>:w=<width>:h=<height>\nffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf \"delogo=x=1236:y=688:w=36:h=22\" -c:a copy clean_output.mp4\n\n# Automated python helper with auto-detection:\nuv run scripts/remove_flow_watermark.py input.mp4 [clean_output.mp4]\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## B-Roll Overlay & Cutaways\n\nInserts a generative Google Flow / Veo 3.1 B-roll clip over the primary voiceover track at a precise timestamp with `setpts=PTS-STARTPTS+T/TB`.\n\n"
  - "### Clean Cutaway with 0.5s Dissolve Fade\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -i main_track.mp4 -i b_roll.mp4 -filter_complex \\\n\"[1:v]scale=1920:1080,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS+15/TB,fade=t=in:st=15:d=0.5:alpha=1,fade=t=out:st=22.5:d=0.5:alpha=1[broll_fade]; \\\n [0:v][broll_fade]overlay=0:0:enable='between(t,15,23)':eof_action=pass[vout]\" \\\n-map \"[vout]\" -map 0:a -c:v libx264 -preset fast -crf 18 -c:a copy final_cutaway.mp4\n```\n\n"
  - "### Picture-in-Picture (PiP) Lower Third Box\n\nScales secondary footage into the bottom right corner with a subtle border:\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -i primary.mp4 -i secondary.mp4 -filter_complex \\\n\"[1:v]scale=480:270,pad=484:274:2:2:white,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS+30/TB[pip]; \\\n [0:v][pip]overlay=W-w-40:H-h-40:enable='between(t,30,55)':eof_action=pass[vout]\" \\\n-map \"[vout]\" -map 0:a -c:v libx264 -c:a copy pip_output.mp4\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Multi-Clip Timeline Concatenation\n\n"
  - "### Lossless Stream Concatenation (Identical Codecs)\n\nCreate file list `inputs.txt`:\n```text\nfile 'scene_01.mp4'\nfile 'scene_02.mp4'\nfile 'scene_03.mp4'\n```\n\nConcatenate without re-encoding:\n```bash\nffmpeg -f concat -safe 0 -i inputs.txt -c copy assembled_full.mp4\n```\n\n"
  - "### Transition Concatenation (Cross-Dissolve xfade)\n\nMerges two scenes with an authentic 1-second film dissolve:\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -i scene_01.mp4 -i scene_02.mp4 -filter_complex \\\n\"[0:v][1:v]xfade=transition=dissolve:duration=1:offset=7[vout]; \\\n [0:a][1:a]acrossfade=d=1[aout]\" \\\n-map \"[vout]\" -map \"[aout]\" -c:v libx264 -crf 18 -c:a aac assembled_dissolve.mp4\n```\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Subtitles & YouTube Export Preset Standards\n\nBurn custom-styled open captions LAST in the filter chain:\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf \\\n\"subtitles=captions.srt:force_style='Fontname=Arial,Fontsize=18,PrimaryColour=&H00FFFFFF,OutlineColour=&H00000000,BorderStyle=3,Outline=2,Shadow=0,Alignment=2,MarginV=40'\" \\\n-c:a copy captioned_output.mp4\n```\n\nYouTube Master Preset (H.264 High Profile Level 4.2, YUV420p, closed GOP, AAC 48kHz):\n```bash\nffmpeg -i master.mp4 -c:v libx264 -profile:v high -level 4.2 -pix_fmt yuv420p -g 30 -bf 2 -crf 17 -preset slow -c:a aac -b:a 384k -ar 48000 youtube_final_master.mp4\n```\n"
